  "h1": "The Sinking City 2 Weapons",
  "seoTitle": "The Sinking City 2 Weapons: Categories and Premium Set",
  "metaDescription": "The Sinking City 2 weapons cover handgun, shotgun, SMG, and revolver categories. Premium Edition adds Shale Mary, The Breakwater, Tektite Tommy, and Bucking Bronco.",
  "summary": "The Sinking City 2 weapons split into four base-game categories - handgun, shotgun, SMG, and revolver - that any edition grants you access to. The Premium Edition adds the Chthonic Arsenal named weapons (Shale Mary handgun, The Breakwater s",
  "hero": {
    "subtitle": "List The Sinking City 2 base-game weapon categories and the Premium-exclusive named weapons.",
    "ctas": []
  },
  "quickAnswer": "The Sinking City 2 weapons split into four base-game categories - handgun, shotgun, SMG, and revolver - that any edition grants you access to. The Premium Edition adds the Chthonic Arsenal named weapons (Shale Mary handgun, The Breakwater shotgun, and Tektite Tommy SMG) and the Holloway Manor side mission's Bucking Bronco revolver, Kane's Hefty Barrel, Kane's Wrapped Grip, and revolver ammo recipe. No named base-game weapon is locked behind the higher tiers; every named premium weapon is a flavored upgrade rather than a required pick.\n\n## The Sinking City 2 Weapons: Base-Game Categories\n\nThe base-game arsenal is organized into four weapon categories: handgun, shotgun, SMG, and revolver. That four-category structure is the core of the survival-horror loadout - you pick a sidearm and a heavier option, and the weapon pickups and crafting recipes you find across the four acts plug into those slots. The category system keeps the inventory shallow enough to manage under pressure while still letting you tune your loadout with the attachments you find or craft.\n\nThe four categories are differentiated by damage profile and ammo economy rather than by progressive \"level\" - a handgun is a fast, low-ammo sidearm for tight corridors and weak-point finishes, a shotgun is the close-range stagger tool, an SMG is your sustained-fire pressure pick when resource counts allow it, and a revolver is the heavy hitter that the Holloway Manor content specifically rewards. The category names appear in the in-game inventory and are the labels the Premium-exclusive named weapons slot into, so Shale Mary is a handgun, The Breakwater is a shotgun, Tektite Tommy is an SMG, and Bucking Bronco is a revolver.\n\nIf you want to know what each category does in practice, the [Sinking City 2 getting started page](/getting-started) covers the resource-management framing that drives category choice, and the [Sinking City 2 walkthrough page](/walkthrough) walks through where each category tends to come online during the four-act campaign. For the opposite side of the equation - what you are firing at - see the [Sinking City 2 enemies page](/enemies).\n\n## Chthonic Arsenal Weapons (Premium-Exclusive)\n\nThe Chthonic Arsenal weapon pack is a Premium Edition exclusive that adds three named weapons across three of the four base-game categories. The pack is included with the Premium Edition digital bundle; it is not sold separately and is not included with the Standard or Deluxe editions. The three weapons are:\n\n- Shale Mary (handgun): a flavored sidearm that slots into the handgun category. Premium-exclusive.\n- The Breakwater (shotgun): a named shotgun that slots into the shotgun category. Premium-exclusive.\n- Tektite Tommy (SMG): a named SMG that slots into the SMG category. Premium-exclusive.\n\nThe Chthonic Arsenal does not add a revolver - the revolver category has its own named reward on the Premium side, which is the Holloway Manor side mission's Bucking Bronco. The three Chthonic Arsenal weapons are factual Premium entitlements, not balance changes: the base-game categories and the Standard / Deluxe edition already give you full access to every weapon category, and the named Chthonic Arsenal weapons are premium-flavored options inside those categories.\n\nThe [Sinking City 2 price page](/price) has the full Premium Edition breakdown, including the 24h early unlock from 17 Aug 2026, the Arkham Field Kit cosmetic pack, and the Holloway Manor side mission that completes the Premium bundle.\n\n## Holloway Manor Weapons and Attachments (Premium-Exclusive)\n\nThe Holloway Manor side mission is the second Premium-exclusive weapon source, and it is the only one that touches the revolver category. Owning the Premium Edition unlocks the side mission, which delivers the named revolver and a small set of revolver-specific attachments and crafting recipe:\n\n- Bucking Bronco revolver: a named revolver that slots into the revolver category. Premium-exclusive.\n- Kane's Hefty Barrel: a revolver attachment dropped as part of the Holloway Manor mission. Premium-exclusive.\n- Kane's Wrapped Grip: a revolver attachment dropped as part of the Holloway Manor mission. Premium-exclusive.\n- Revolver ammo recipe: a crafting recipe rewarded in the Holloway Manor mission. Premium-exclusive.\n\nThe Holloway Manor mission is a discrete side mission rather than a passive drop, so the Bucking Bronco and the Kane's attachments are gated behind actually playing through the mission rather than simply owning the edition. The revolver ammo recipe is the most tactically meaningful of the four because it lets you refill revolver ammo without scavenging, which is the kind of recipe that decides whether the revolver is a luxury pick or a sustained option in the late acts.\n\nBecause Holloway Manor is a Premium addition, the revolver category is the only category that has a named reward entirely on the Premium side. If you are on Standard or Deluxe, the revolver category still works - you can pick up and use a revolver - but you will not get the named Bucking Bronco or the revolver ammo recipe, and the Kane's attachments will not appear in your inventory.\n\n## Attachment System Overview\n\nEvery base-game weapon category accepts attachments, and the attachment system is the most important customization layer in the late acts. Attachments are found as loot drops across districts, purchased or earned through Investigation side missions, and - in the Premium tier - awarded as named rewards from the Holloway Manor mission. The two Kane's attachments are the only named attachment rewards in the Holloway Manor set; most attachments are unnamed and are picked up as you explore.\n\nThe attachment system is what makes the category choice feel consequential. The same handgun can be tuned for damage, control, or ammo efficiency depending on which attachment you slot; the same shotgun can be tuned for tighter spread or higher per-shot damage. If you are budgeting your time, the practical implication is that the resource-vs-avoidance trade-off covered on the [Sinking City 2 enemies page](/enemies) is mediated by attachments more than by named weapons, because attachments are what let you stretch a limited ammo economy across the four acts.\n\nNamed weapons from the Chthonic Arsenal and Holloway Manor are tuned differently from base-game pickups but are not categorically stronger across the board - they are flavored loadout options. The real scaling in the late game comes from the attachment system and the ammo recipes you unlock, including the revolver ammo recipe from Holloway Manor.",
