  "h1": "The Sinking City 2 Endings",
  "seoTitle": "The Sinking City 2 Endings and Legacy Boundary",
  "metaDescription": "The Sinking City 2 endings detail is not yet documented post-launch. This page marks the boundary with the original 2019 Oakmont ending coverage.",
  "summary": "The Sinking City 2 endings are not yet documented in the launch press packet as of 2026-08-18. The four-act main story closes in the late regions, but the specific ending count, the choice points, and any branching consequence have not been",
  "hero": {
    "subtitle": "Find The Sinking City 2 ending(s) and how they differ from The Sinking City 1's Oakmont endings.",
    "ctas": []
  },
  "quickAnswer": "The Sinking City 2 endings are not yet documented in the launch press packet as of 2026-08-18. The four-act main story closes in the late regions, but the specific ending count, the choice points, and any branching consequence have not been published by Frogwares or the launch press. This page marks the boundary: the original 2019 Oakmont ending coverage belongs on the [Sinking City 2 vs The Sinking City 1 page](/vs-the-sinking-city-1), not here.\n\n## The Sinking City 2 Endings: Current Status\n\nThe Sinking City 2 endings are not yet documented as of 2026-08-18. The launch press coverage - PCGamer (Jody Macgregor), Rock Paper Shotgun, wccftech, SixthAxis, and the OpenCritic 40-critic aggregate with a Strong 81 rating - focuses on the four-act main story structure, the Cal Rafferty and Faye Bennett storyline, and the survival-horror combat loop. None of the launch press packet enumerates the specific ending count, the choice points that lead to each ending, or the branching structure of the final beats.\n\nThe current-game ending detail is post-launch coverage work. The practical implication is that this page does not invent ending counts, choice points, or branching conditions, because the source tier for those facts would be community playthroughs and wiki entries rather than the Steam store, the Frogwares official channels, or the launch press. The launch press frame is clear: the four-act main story closes in the late regions, and the Cal Rafferty and Faye Bennett storyline is the spine of the campaign.\n\nFor the four-act structure and the resource checkpoints that the final beats sit on, see the [Sinking City 2 walkthrough page](/walkthrough). For the Cal Rafferty and Faye Bennett storyline that the endings resolve, see the [Sinking City 2 setting and Arkham page](/setting-arkham). The [Sinking City 2 vs The Sinking City 1 page](/vs-the-sinking-city-1) covers the boundary between the current-game ending coverage and the 2019 Oakmont ending coverage.\n\n## Legacy Boundary with The Sinking City 1\n\nThis page covers only the current game's endings. The Sinking City 1 (2019) is a separate title with its own ending coverage, and the boundary between the two is intentional. The 2019 game used an open-world detective structure with Charles Reed as the protagonist and a sanity meter mechanic; its ending coverage belongs to the comparison page rather than to this reference page.\n\nLegacy reference (The Sinking City, 2019): Oakmont was the 1920s flooded city Charles Reed investigated, and the 2019 game's ending coverage is documented across the 2019 fan base and the 2025 Remastered edition's re-release. The 2019 ending coverage is not a current-game source of facts, and it is not the answer to the question \"what are The Sinking City 2 endings?\". The 2019 coverage is part of the comparison context, not part of the current coverage.\n\nThe boundary matters because the 2019 original has a well-known ending structure and a fan base that remembers it. Anyone searching for \"The Sinking City 2 endings\" is likely to find 2019 content in the same search results, and that 2019 content can be mistaken for current-game coverage. The boundary is explicit: current-game facts belong on this page, 2019 Oakmont coverage belongs on the [Sinking City 2 vs The Sinking City 1 page](/vs-the-sinking-city-1), and there is no overlap in the source-tier rules.\n\nThe 2019 original's ending coverage is acknowledged here as a legacy reference so that the 2019 reader can find the comparison material, and the 2019 boundaries are explicit so that the 2026 reader does not mistake 2019 ending structure for 2026 ending structure. The boundary does not predict that the 2026 game will or will not share ending structure with the 2019 game - it only notes that the comparison belongs on the comparison page.\n\n## New Game Plus Behavior Note\n\nPCGamer's launch review notes that New Game Plus does not let you keep progress. That detail is community-relevant because it tells a player who is planning to see the endings that NG+ is not a route to a \"second ending run with full loadout\" - it is a restart of the four-act campaign without carried-over unlocks. The NG+ detail is also a reason the current-game ending coverage stays open: with NG+ as a restart rather than a continue, the ending coverage that matters is the first-playthrough ending set, not a second-playthrough variant set.\n\nThe practical reading of the NG+ detail is that a player who wants to see the endings should focus on the first playthrough rather than save a second run for NG+. The ending count, the choice points, and the branching consequences are not yet documented, so the planning advice is straightforward: play the first playthrough carefully rather than rely on NG+ as a safety net. The [Sinking City 2 walkthrough page](/walkthrough) covers the four-act progression where the ending choices appear, and the [Sinking City 2 updates and DLC page](/updates-dlc) is the place where any post-launch NG+ adjustments would be flagged.\n\nThe NG+ behavior is a single fact from PCGamer's launch review, not a developer-published NG+ specification. The launch press does not list every NG+ carry-over item, and the developer has not published a detailed NG+ FAQ. The current-game ending coverage will be the place where the actual ending set is documented once the post-launch coverage exists.\n\n## Post-Launch Coverage Plan\n\nThe post-launch coverage plan for The Sinking City 2 endings is to wait for one of three sources to publish the specifics: the Frogwares official channel (YouTube, Kickstarter updates, or the developer site), the launch press reaching a longer-form write-up that walks through the final beats, or a screenshot-confirmed playthrough that names the choices and branches. Until one of those three sources lands, this page stays at the current status: ending count not documented, choice points not documented, branching consequences not documented.\n\nThe post-launch coverage plan is also a tracker for three related items: the exact ending count, the location of any choice points in the four-act structure, and whether any post-launch DLC would add additional endings. All three are post-launch unknowns and the coverage will not invent them. The [Sinking City 2 updates and DLC page](/updates-dlc) is the place where any DLC that would add ending content would be flagged first, and the [Sinking City 2 walkthrough page](/walkthrough) is the place where the ending walkthrough itself would be published once the coverage exists.\n\nThe reader-facing version of the post-launch plan is simple: check back, watch the Steam News feed, and watch the Frogwares YouTube channel for an official document. The third-party fan wiki `thesinkingcity-2.wiki` is treated as `community/video`-tier only and is not the source of truth for ending counts. Ending coverage that requires community playthroughs will be flagged as community-attributed rather than as confirmed.",
