  "h1": "The Sinking City 2 Arkham Setting",
  "seoTitle": "The Sinking City 2 Arkham Setting and Protagonists",
  "metaDescription": "The Sinking City 2 Arkham setting is 1920s Lovecraftian America. Cal Rafferty investigates while Faye Bennett is trapped in the Dreamlands; dev is Frogwares.",
  "summary": "The Sinking City 2 Arkham setting drops you into a 1920s Lovecraftian American port city under supernatural flood. Calvin \"Cal\" Rafferty is the confirmed protagonist; Faye Bennett is confirmed supporting cast, her soul trapped in the Dreaml",
  "hero": {
    "subtitle": "Understand the 1920s Arkham setting, Cal Rafferty, Faye Bennett, and Frogwares's connection to the original game.",
    "ctas": []
  },
  "quickAnswer": "The Sinking City 2 Arkham setting drops you into a 1920s Lovecraftian American port city under supernatural flood. Calvin \"Cal\" Rafferty is the confirmed protagonist; Faye Bennett is confirmed supporting cast, her soul trapped in the Dreamlands while her body has been stolen. Frogwares Ireland Ltd. develops and publishes the game; the studio also made the 2019 Oakmont original and the 2025 Remastered edition. The setting shift from Oakmont to Arkham is a deliberate sequel move.\n\n## The Sinking City 2 Arkham Setting: 1920s Lovecraftian America\n\nThe Sinking City 2 Arkham setting is a 1920s American port city that has been hit by a supernatural flood. The setting is a Lovecraftian mythology frame: the city is a real place - not Arkham, Massachusetts from the original Lovecraft stories, but a Frogwares-built Arkham that lives in the same 1920s Lovecraftian America - and the supernatural flood is the disaster that the four-act campaign is built around. The tide-stained avenues, the flooded streets, and the boat navigation between districts are the visual and mechanical signs that the city is the antagonist as much as the enemies are.\n\nThe 1920s setting is doing several jobs at once. It is the costume drama backdrop - you will see Prohibition-era city design, period-appropriate interiors, and the kind of speakeasy and street texture that defines the decade. It is the historical frame for the survival-horror resource economy - the four acts are built around a city that has been hit by a disaster, not a city in peacetime. It is also the Lovecraftian hook: the 1920s are the decade the original Lovecraft stories take place in, and the setting reads as a deliberate mythology choice rather than a generic period backdrop.\n\n## Cal Rafferty: The Confirmed Protagonist\n\nCalvin \"Cal\" Rafferty is the confirmed protagonist of The Sinking City 2. Cal is the player character, and the four-act campaign is told from his perspective. The Cal Rafferty storyline is the spine of the campaign: he arrives in the flooded Arkham, he investigates the supernatural events, and the Faye Bennett storyline is the relationship that drives the late acts. Cal is the character you play; the player-character role is the only role that is fully confirmed across the launch press.\n\nThe shift from Charles Reed to Cal Rafferty is a deliberate sequel move. Charles Reed was the protagonist of the 2019 original (an open-world detective) and Cal Rafferty is the protagonist of the current title (a survival-horror investigator). The investigative frame is preserved, but the genre shift from open-world detective to survival-horror action changes what Cal Rafferty actually does in the four acts: he fights, he manages resources, he makes the survival-horror trade-offs, and he resolves the Faye Bennett storyline.\n\nThe Cal Rafferty role is the only fully confirmed character role. Any \"named cast beyond Cal Rafferty and Faye Bennett\" is not documented in the launch press packet. The [Sinking City 2 walkthrough page](/walkthrough) covers where Cal Rafferty shows up in the four-act progression, and this page covers the character setup that the four-act story is built around.\n\n## Faye Bennett: Supporting Role, Confirmed\n\nFaye Bennett is the confirmed supporting cast. Faye Bennett's situation is the most distinctive part of the current game's character setup: her soul is trapped in the Dreamlands, and her body has been stolen. The Dreamlands is the Lovecraftian mythology frame for a parallel dimension, and the body-theft frame is the kind of mythology-meets-mystery setup that the 1920s Lovecraftian setting exists to support. Faye Bennett's arc is the relationship that drives the late acts.\n\nThe Faye Bennett role is the only other confirmed character role. The launch press does not enumerate any other named cast beyond Cal Rafferty and Faye Bennett, and the launch press does not describe the specific ways Faye shows up in the in-game narrative. The Dreamlands mechanics are not documented in the launch press packet, and any specific Dreamlands-driving gameplay element is post-launch coverage work rather than current-game fact.\n\nFaye Bennett's supporting role is the anchor for the late-arc storyline. The four-act structure uses Cal Rafferty as the player-character vessel and the Faye Bennett storyline as the relationship that the late acts pay off. The specific payoff is part of the current-game ending detail that is not yet documented and is covered on the [Sinking City 2 endings page](/endings).\n\n## Frogwares Ireland Ltd.: The Developer\n\nThe Sinking City 2 is developed and self-published by Frogwares Ireland Ltd. Frogwares is a Ukrainian-founded studio that operates as an Irish entity, and the company self-publishes the current game. Frogwares is the developer behind the 2019 original The Sinking City, the 2025 Remastered edition, and a series of Sherlock Holmes titles that established the studio's investigative-game pedigree. The current game is the studio's return to the survival-horror investigative frame.\n\nThe developer identity is the continuity between the 2019 original and the current title. The 2019 original was a Frogwares title, and the 2025 Remastered edition was a Frogwares title. The current title is the studio's next major Lovecraftian release, and the developer connection is why the comparison page is structured around \"Frogwares 2019 Oakmont vs Frogwares 2026 Arkham\" rather than around a studio change.\n\nThe developer context also frames the release. The 2026-08-18 worldwide release, the Premium 24h early unlock from 2026-08-17, and the gold master build on 2026-08-07 are all Frogwares-supplied milestones that the launch press and the Steam store carry.\n\n## Comparison to The Sinking City 1's Oakmont\n\nThe current title shifts the setting from Oakmont to Arkham. The 2019 original was set in Oakmont, a 1920s flooded city investigated by Charles Reed, and the sanity meter was the signature mechanic that tied the setting to the gameplay. The current title is set in Arkham, a 1920s flooded city investigated by Cal Rafferty, and the survival-horror resource economy is the new spine. The setting shift is a deliberate sequel move - the 1920s Lovecraftian frame is preserved, but the city is new and the protagonist is new.\n\nThe comparison is the easiest way to read the setting update. Cal Rafferty's survival-horror investigation is the new shape of the 1920s Lovecraftian game, and the developer connection is what makes the comparison meaningful. The 2019 original's Oakmont coverage is part of the [Sinking City 2 vs The Sinking City 1 page](/vs-the-sinking-city-1), and the boundary between the two is explicit: the 2019 original's Oakmont is a legacy reference, and the current title's Arkham is the current-game setting.\n\nThe setting comparison is not a value judgment. The 2019 original is its own game, and the 2025 Remastered edition is its own re-release. The current title's Arkham setting is the frame for the four-act Cal Rafferty and Faye Bennett storyline, and the boundary between legacy Oakmont coverage and current Arkham coverage is the disambiguation the launch press and the comparison page both rely on.",
